# 6. GAMEPLAY AND COMBAT SYSTEM

Build a functional FPS shooting system.

## A. First-Person Camera

Use a Three.js PerspectiveCamera.

The camera represents the player's point of view.

The player should see:

- Environment.
- Incoming zombies.
- Weapon or weapon placeholder.
- Crosshair.
- Visual shooting effects.

Implement responsive canvas resizing.

## B. Weapon System

Implement a simple weapon system.

Features:

- Weapon visible in the foreground.
- Shooting animation or recoil.
- Muzzle flash.
- Shooting cooldown.
- Gunshot sound.
- Hit feedback.
- Configurable fire rate.

Start with one weapon.

Do not spend excessive time implementing multiple weapon classes.

If ammunition and reload mechanics are implemented, include an adjustable magazine size and reload action. Mouse/keyboard reload must remain available as a fallback.

## C. Raycasting

Use Three.js Raycaster to detect shots.

The ray must originate from the camera and follow the current crosshair position.

When a shot is fired:

1. Convert crosshair coordinates to normalized device coordinates.
2. Construct a ray from the camera.
3. Check collision against zombie hitboxes.
4. Apply damage if a zombie is hit.
5. Update score and accuracy.
6. Trigger appropriate visual and audio feedback.

Use simplified invisible hitboxes.

Do not check every detailed polygon of every zombie mesh unnecessarily.

## D. Zombie AI

Implement basic zombie behavior:

- Idle.
- Spawn.
- Walk toward the player.
- Attack when sufficiently close.
- Receive damage.
- Hit reaction.
- Death.

For the MVP, use simple movement and state-based AI.

No advanced pathfinding or complicated physics are required.

Zombies should:
- Spawn at predefined positions.
- Approach the player.
- Cause damage when reaching the attack distance.
- Have configurable health and speed.
- Be removed or pooled after death.

Create different spawn positions to avoid all zombies appearing in one location.

## E. Player Health

Implement a player health system.

When zombies reach attack distance:
- Trigger an attack.
- Reduce player health.
- Play the appropriate attack sound.
- Show visual damage feedback.

When health reaches zero, end the mission as failed.

